---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/";
---
<Layout title="RLCIE Business Development Manager — Rahul Jain">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href={base + "origins/"}>&larr; Origins</a>
    <h1 class="page-title">Business Development On-Campus Manager</h1>
    <p class="page-lede"><a href="https://www.cmc.edu/rlcie" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Randall Lewis Center for Innovation &amp; Entrepreneurship (RLCIE)<Icon name="external" /></a>, Claremont McKenna College &middot; 2020&ndash;2022</p>
    <section>
      <p class="blurb">
        One of five campus leads — one per Claremont college — on the RLCIE leadership team. The role was
        essentially <strong>business development for student entrepreneurship</strong>: I served as the student liaison
        between RLCIE and the entrepreneurial community on my campus, which meant a few concrete things.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Identifying startups and student entrepreneurs on campus, often before they had any formal visibility.</li>
        <li>Promoting RLCIE events, resources, and the RLCIE marketplace to that community.</li>
        <li>Evaluating what founders actually needed and connecting them to people in the RLCIE network — on campus or off — who could help.</li>
        <li>Recruiting and leading a small team of students to build up specific knowledge of how startups function, so we could meaningfully consult with founders rather than just refer them elsewhere.</li>
        <li>Building partnership opportunities between RLCIE and other entrepreneurship-focused groups across the 5Cs, like The Hive, Pomona Ventures, and Kravis Labs.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="blurb">
        It was a role built on the same skill as everything on this page: <strong>figuring out what a person
        actually needs</strong>, then finding or building the connection that gets them there.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
